@* Logout.razor — Phase 1.2
   Static-rendered logout endpoint. Clears the auth cookie and redirects
   to /Account/Login with forceLoad:true.

   WHY STATIC (not Blazor circuit):
     Same reason as Login.razor — the cookie clear must happen on the
     HTTP response, which requires static SSR. A Blazor circuit call
     to SignInManager.SignOutAsync would write the cookie-clear headers
     to the circuit's response, which is not the same as the browser's
     HTTP response. The next request would still carry the old cookie.

   WHY A RAZOR PAGE (not a controller endpoint):
     The simplest pattern in Blazor Server is to use a static-rendered
     .razor page with @page "/Account/Logout" and just call SignOutAsync
     in OnInitialized. No separate MVC controller needed.

   FLOW:
     1. User clicks the logout button in MainLayout (which navigates to
        /Account/Logout with forceLoad:true).
     2. This page receives the request (static SSR — no circuit).
     3. OnInitialized runs SignInManager.SignOutAsync, which clears the
        auth cookie.
     4. Navigation.NavigateTo("/Account/Login", forceLoad:true) sends
        a 302 to the browser. The new request has no cookie → user
        sees the login page. *@

@page "/Account/Logout"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity
@using TakOne.Infrastructure.Identity
@inject SignInManager<ApplicationUser> SignInManager
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IHttpContextAccessor HttpContextAccessor

@code {
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        var httpContext = HttpContextAccessor.HttpContext;

        // SignOutAsync clears the auth cookie. It also clears any
        // external-cookie-derived identity (we don't have any external
        // logins in v1, but the call is safe regardless).
        if (httpContext is not null)
        {
            await SignInManager.SignOutAsync();
        }

        // Force a full HTTP round-trip — the next request must NOT
        // carry the cookie. If we used client-side Blazor navigation
        // here, the circuit might still see the pre-logout auth state
        // and bounce the user back to the dashboard.
        Navigation.NavigateTo("/Account/Login", forceLoad: true);
    }
}